\title{Continuous Map}
\taxon{Definition}
\p{
    Let #{(X,\tau_X)} and #{(Y,\tau_Y)} be [topological spaces](def-000C). A
    map #{f:X\to Y} is \strong{continuous} if the preimage of every open set
    is open:
    ##{
        V\in\tau_Y
        \quad\Longrightarrow\quad
        f^{-1}(V)\in\tau_X.
    }
    Equivalently, the preimage of every closed subset of #{Y} is closed in
    #{X}. Continuity therefore depends on both the underlying function and the
    topologies placed on its domain and codomain.
}
